# Coveted Jewel: "Whenever one or more creatures an opponent controls attack you and aren't blocked, that player draws three cards and
# gains control of this artifact. Untap it." In a three-player game Bot1 casts the Jewel on turn 1 (Black Lotus and three Moxen) and
# Bot2's Llanowar Elves attacks Bot1 unblocked on turn 5. With the trigger on the stack Bot2 concedes and leaves the game (CR 104.3a,
# 800.4a). The trigger still resolves, but the Jewel would change to the control of a player who has left the game, so it doesn't
# (CR 800.4b): it stays Bot1's, and the game goes on between Bot1 and Bot3.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Jet
Mox Pearl
Mox Sapphire
Coveted Jewel
Plains x15

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Llanowar Elves
Forest x16

[Bot3 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Black)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Coveted Jewel.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
[T5 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Attack(Llanowar Elves > Bot1)
[T5 Bot2.Blockers]
Bot2.Concede
[T5 Bot2.Main2]

[Expect]
Result = InProgress
Bot1.Battlefield = Mox Jet; Mox Pearl; Mox Sapphire; Coveted Jewel
Bot1.Battlefield.Coveted Jewel.Tapped = false
Bot2.Battlefield.Count = 0
